00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Boy meets girl. Girl unimpressed. Boy starts band.

2
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Sing Street is a romance, drama, music film directed by John Carney.

3
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:36,000
A boy growing up in Dublin during the 1980s escapes his strained family life
by starting a band to impress the mysterious girl he likes.

4
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Conor "Cosmo" Lawlor, played by Ferdia Walsh-Peelo.

5
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Raphina, played by Lucy Boynton.

6
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Brendan Lawlor, played by Jack Reynor.

7
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:56,000
Darren, played by Ben Carolan.

8
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Eamon, played by Mark McKenna.

9
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Ann Lawlor, played by Kelly Thornton.

10
00:58:20,000 --> 00:58:26,000
Sing Street is a 2016 coming-of-age musical comedy-drama film written and
directed by John Carney from a story by Carney and Simon Carmody.

11
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
Starring Lucy Boynton, Maria Doyle Kennedy, Aidan Gillen, Jack Reynor, Kelly Thornton and Ferdia Walsh-Peelo,
the story revolves around a teenage boy who forms a band to impress a girl in 1980s Dublin.

12
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
It is an international co-production of Ireland, the
United Kingdom and the United States.

13
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
The film had its world premiere at the Sundance
Film Festival on 24 January 2016.

14
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
It was released in Ireland on 17 March 2016, in the United States
on 15 April and in the United Kingdom on 20 May.

15
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
The film received positive reviews from critics, grossed $13.6 million worldwide on a $4 million budget, and
was nominated for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy at the 74th Golden Globe Awards.

16
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
The film explores themes of friendship, london, england,
sibling relationship, dublin, ireland, music video.

17
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:16,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
